From 7702a67d1f0bb05a7bd91e1cf356c15b7d20d8ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:50:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): paint external-run cards sky/red with service
 hover [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Session stripe gains external (sky-400 / dark sky-500) and external_down
(red-500) with a cloud glyph (hollow when unknown). Precedence is ⌘B >
live turn > stuck/red including external_down > external > stalled >
waiting > done. Kanban scheduled+external is "running externally"; down
is red. Hover names the service and status per interface-hover.md;
sidebar lists kanban_external_cards (max 5 + "+N more"). Absent fields
keep today's output.

Proof:
- vitest 153 passed (external-run, stripe colour, precedence, badge,
  meter, hover running/queued/unknown/down/+N more/missing-field)
- tsc --noEmit clean; eslint clean on touched files
- python3 scripts/check --only health ok
- fixtures only (no live backend)

Existing kanbanStripeCounts toEqual tests grew extra zero keys because
the return object now includes external/externalDown/externalUnknown.
Meter toEqual similarly gained external/externalDown zeros.

Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.6 <noreply@x.ai>
